# Firewall adoption and recovery

## Adopt the current firewall

Follow [Adopt existing settings](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/elephant-evergreen/synology/latest/docs/resources/firewall#adopt-existing-settings) for the copyable configuration and import-only plan.

Import reads the profile without saving it, activating it, or stopping a task. Destroy releases Terraform management and leaves the policy installed.

## Change the selected profile

1. Verify an independent management path before editing rules. Use a direct certificate-valid DSM endpoint on DSM's native HTTPS port. Verify the actual connection path as well as the port.
2. After adoption, run `terraform state show synology_firewall.nas` to read the profile and `adapters` policy. Use your actual resource address if it differs. For an enabled policy, keep DSM port checking enabled and set `management_networks` to the administrator source CIDRs DSM sees after NAT or VPN translation.
3. For each management network, place an explicit global allow for the DSM HTTPS port before matching denies or uncertain selectors. The provider refuses early GeoIP, service-name, source-port or partial-range selectors when it cannot prove management access.
4. Edit the adopted resource using your profile and complete adapter policy, including the rules you want to keep.
5. Save the plan with `terraform plan -out=firewall.tfplan`. Apply it with `terraform apply firewall.tfplan` only if it contains the intended policy and rule order.
6. Verify DSM access from the intended networks.

